    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d406">

                <pb facs="0397" n="281" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg281"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 437.00/32.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 138.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 5, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to previous correspondence in
                    regard to the so-called “insurrectionary claims” against Cuba, and particularly
                    to <pb facs="0398" n="282" xml:id="pg282"/> my despatch No. 104 of the 12th
                    ultimo, I have the honor to transmit herewith enclosed copy and translation of a
                    personal note and enclosure received from Sr. Sanguily, wherein he informs me as
                    to the more recent developments in his negotiations with the representatives of
                    the three interested powers.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. M. Beaupré</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d406-a1.xml" xpointer="d406-a1"/>
